><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D45D TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"3\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2B\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"3\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c37\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml display=\"inline\" unselectable=\"on\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></div></div></div>, which is an integer.</div><div class=\"answerDetails\"><div class=\"questionDifficulty difficultyEasy\">E</div><span class=\"answerCreated\">Sat, Oct 10th @ 9:56 PM</span><span class=\"answerDetailsSeparator\">|</span><span class=\"timeElpased\">Elapsed: 6:25</span><span class=\"answerResult\"><span style=\"color: green;\">Correct</span></span></div></div>"
      },
      {
        "dom_id": "question-183996",
        "name": null,
        "problem": "Suppose $n=10m-2,$ where $m\\in Z.$ Complete the following argument showing that $n$ is even.",
        "worked_solution": "An integer is *even* if it can be written as $2a,$ where $a$ is an integer.\n\nTherefore, we complete our argument as follows:\n\nThe number $n$ is even since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =10m-2 \\\\  & =2({{5m-1}_{⏟}}_{a}) \\\\  & =2a,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere we have defined $a=5m-1,$ which is an integer.",
        "calculator_instructions": "",
        "fields": [
          {
            "key": "field-1",
            "type": "select",
            "dom_id": "selectList-183996-0",
            "tag": "custom-select",
            "choices": [
              {
                "option": "0",
                "dom_id": null,
